id: SCA-068
title: DNS exfiltration pattern
category: supply-chain
severity: error
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .sh .bash .py .js .ts
  exclude_paths: test/ node_modules/ .git/ vendor/
patterns:
  - regex: (dig|nslookup|host)\s+.*\$
    message: DNS query with interpolated variable — attackers encode stolen data (tokens, credentials) as DNS query labels, exfiltrating through DNS which bypasses firewalls.
  - regex: \.burpcollaborator\.net|\.oast\.|\.interact\.sh
    message: Known exfiltration domain detected — burpcollaborator.net, oast, and interact.sh are used for out-of-band data exfiltration.
fix: DNS queries with interpolated variables are a strong exfiltration indicator. Remove and investigate. Block known exfiltration domains at the network level.
